#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184172 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184071 :question/id #uuid "78547385-d46f-5a2a-bfc1-39e040208ca0" :question/math-academy-id "e-5426" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and  \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\left\\{ \\left. \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\;\\right| \\;x_1, x_3 \\in\\mathbb{R} \\right\\}?\n$$\n\n \n\nI. $\\textrm{rank}(A)=1$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is a $2$-dimensional subspace of $\\Bbb R^3$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n\n\n$$\nA \\textrm{ is invertible} \\qquad \\Leftrightarrow \\qquad \\left\\{\\; \\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={\\mathbb{R}}^{3} \\\\ & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\mathbf{0}\\} \\\\ & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned} \\right.\n$$\n\n\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A) + \\textrm{nullity}(A) = n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that \n\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\textrm{Span}\\left\\{ {\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} }\\right\\}\n$$\n\n \nwhich means that $\\textrm{nullity}(A) =2.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n = 3,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =3 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\textrm{nullity}(A) = 2 \\neq 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ cannot be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\textrm{rank}(A) = 1,$ we have that $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is a $1$-dimensional subspace of $\\Bbb R^3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e145cb2-806a-579d-8299-8a91a6feaad1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049340 :topic/difficulty 0.5118524148844472 :topic/id #uuid "ecf075bf-6d18-5a77-93a9-57ef73f45115" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124630}] :topic/math-academy-id 1869 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048978} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050001}] :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Dimension, Rank and Nullity"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673453 :question-generator/id #uuid "9c1c0a10-9e58-5008-b31c-351d13a59be1" :question-generator/script "generators/8d/8d9a00edf3f8741e7093fba9b37ff5eff6f36d0192b1dba2a5c5eaeccb56cbd8/17592186184172.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a17adadd-02fe-5b13-a556-c4b68557dec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183140} {:answer/id #uuid "f44f8717-6bc7-5c29-a85d-01286768fa78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183141} {:answer/id #uuid "3493b4eb-bc91-59c3-abe3-1362d436c2d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183142} {:answer/id #uuid "3d5d43af-17a2-5f2e-916b-b2453eace3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183143} {:answer/id #uuid "62186aa1-6d7f-5a56-8e00-28c657c126cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f44f8717-6bc7-5c29-a85d-01286768fa78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183141} :answer-field/id #uuid "405282dd-7ce6-56bf-8492-d4b7cbb14f8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183139}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4d185801-460b-5883-a896-8f1107477aa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-34930" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\}?\n$$\n\nI. The number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $3$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since the generating vectors in \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nare linearly independent, we conclude that the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=2\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=4.$ Now, according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184757 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148c103f-607d-5f86-b626-7f905a9009be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183152} {:answer/id #uuid "1a5566c6-f36e-5fa6-963f-ff29a059239e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183153} {:answer/id #uuid "1eee22c0-aaee-5c76-b935-89d9e34d716f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183154} {:answer/id #uuid "21dd967c-ba0d-5081-815f-e4707b87b16d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183155} {:answer/id #uuid "6a680598-5a75-5f51-afed-93c0cd66c558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a5566c6-f36e-5fa6-963f-ff29a059239e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183153} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c0659d5-6754-5a2c-b59d-a8d4e248b40e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183151}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50dd3dbf-46fe-5a60-971b-ec20882fc4a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-34934" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix with $3$ pivot columns?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=4.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have that $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =4 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c2659df-70b4-5256-87fa-2a34198af876" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449658} {:answer/id #uuid "77a2cd60-bf16-5a97-b3a5-f6ed36dd706c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77a2cd60-bf16-5a97-b3a5-f6ed36dd706c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449659} :answer-field/id #uuid "3592b310-da06-5773-8430-cf897b63efce" :answer-field/key "$A$ is  **not** invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450783} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71487a84-b41a-585b-8ff3-f6fbfac9393d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449660} {:answer/id #uuid "dc36f444-1255-5d82-87f6-8355261ee483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc36f444-1255-5d82-87f6-8355261ee483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449661} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d161315-6d73-5e59-8ca0-0d5fd8273d52" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0d44763-7df9-5816-b934-fe067cf8d583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449662} {:answer/id #uuid "3786226d-53c4-521c-afec-80c21f875609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0d44763-7df9-5816-b934-fe067cf8d583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449662} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c5e784e-a241-51f7-84ca-848b80cea623" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450785}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a4ded73-dd50-5431-9dd3-a7f4831d94c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-142544" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix which has only $3$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{7} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=7=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is  **not** invertible” is true. Since $A$ has $n=7$ columns and $3$ of them is a non-pivot one, it follows that    \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Col}(A))=7-3=4\\ne 7.\n$$\n\n Thus,  according to the invertible matrix theorem $A$ is  **not** an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$” is true.  Indeed, since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=\\text{rank}(A)=4$,  then $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$ is false. Since $n=7$, according to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =7 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =7-4 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is  **not** invertible”; “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d0391e2-c7ef-5a32-a6e4-a1dd2f23ab04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449664} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6ce1e9-a2d9-513e-9218-2fe7d1e0a8a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d0391e2-c7ef-5a32-a6e4-a1dd2f23ab04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449664} :answer-field/id #uuid "0aed2ada-8cf1-5887-add8-5891a536ebb4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450786} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1af8c890-adc0-5501-b776-d23219000bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449666} {:answer/id #uuid "78ea7642-4a88-5dd4-9c0e-b9cddd5255a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1af8c890-adc0-5501-b776-d23219000bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449666} :answer-field/id #uuid "e11f78a0-08ce-50e3-88fc-e1011761342e" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "634c8a5c-c46d-507d-a2df-cc1a7726c974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449668} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3e28a0-079e-52e9-9123-05a2f2341769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d3e28a0-079e-52e9-9123-05a2f2341769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449669} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6e79aa7-abeb-5d53-9e24-d52f8f63b70a" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450788}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5342a760-4f6b-57f7-989c-35eadd9600b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-143533" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b\\in R\\right\\}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{3} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=3=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$  \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b\\in R\\right\\}=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\,\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=3,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =3 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=2\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement $det(A)=0$ is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible we must have   $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $det(A)=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348221 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5eb0fdb-7256-54c3-9a7a-a9dca48fc612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451741} {:answer/id #uuid "81ce3ea0-81f7-5844-b779-4c3cea386177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ce3ea0-81f7-5844-b779-4c3cea386177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451742} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac36175b-5342-5095-991f-b0d75bb31fa9" :answer-field/key "$A$ is  **not** invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452718} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7348cde9-7949-5bff-82b0-8b60d1a6b39f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451743} {:answer/id #uuid "01621a61-e00e-5295-bb23-ab9f96754ed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7348cde9-7949-5bff-82b0-8b60d1a6b39f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451743} :answer-field/id #uuid "29d3a068-4e65-58a9-a0c0-45461411dede" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $2$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452719} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f1ec200-5f46-55a8-a21f-13735ffe254a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451745} {:answer/id #uuid "6075a26d-50e6-543d-90ef-7a1fbac5e9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6075a26d-50e6-543d-90ef-7a1fbac5e9be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451746} :answer-field/id #uuid "12403c46-08ab-5006-baea-a3791d434532" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452720}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "322fb855-3d8d-59e6-ba9e-0f5421e84a86" :question/math-academy-id "q-79417" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix which has only $1$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is  **not** invertible” is true. Since $A$ has $n=5$ columns and $1$ of them is a non-pivot one, it follows that    \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5-1=4\\ne 5.\n$$\n\n Thus, according to the invertible matrix theorem $A$ is  **not** an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $2$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$” is false. Since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=\\text{rank}(A)=4$,  then $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $4$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$ is true. Indeed, since $n=5$, according to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is  **not** invertible”; $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c56bbd1f-d979-5241-8dc4-a8e64037e678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451747} {:answer/id #uuid "b5789825-466e-5d22-9f09-42c97e0435a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c56bbd1f-d979-5241-8dc4-a8e64037e678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451747} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cc17da3-e4d0-5047-880f-6b1aaa55e9cb" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452721} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e85400e8-1b39-5381-89d4-9456a7b1822c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451749} {:answer/id #uuid "a330ce1f-b4c7-5d2b-9114-283fa3e27999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a330ce1f-b4c7-5d2b-9114-283fa3e27999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451750} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fca603b-0e04-57c7-b9ac-a845c8d3054f" :answer-field/key "$A$ is not  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452722} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47f7bb58-5fc7-50bf-bcf6-b8a2a3b9a52d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451751} {:answer/id #uuid "927e07de-2922-5088-8e17-5260e4060177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "927e07de-2922-5088-8e17-5260e4060177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451752} :answer-field/id #uuid "6904f830-30a3-5787-9c3c-630ff0631353" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452723}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "251cb9e2-c851-5082-b166-e39206cbabf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-79420" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix with only  $1$ pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=4=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is false. Since $A$ has just $1$ pivot column, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=1.$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is not  invertible” is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=4.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$ is true. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 1+\\text{nullity}(A) & =4 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is not  invertible”; $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da20820a-7cf1-52ba-a9b8-2212f98fa16b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451753} {:answer/id #uuid "7aefb362-63f4-504f-98b5-a2da25f151f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da20820a-7cf1-52ba-a9b8-2212f98fa16b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451753} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c53c77e-992f-545f-ba55-2353aade2814" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9882f7d4-51ae-5c58-b561-ff060c844fd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451755} {:answer/id #uuid "2541f8cb-7e6a-5880-81b4-5ca6877fea1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2541f8cb-7e6a-5880-81b4-5ca6877fea1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451756} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6fdddfe-e700-5aea-b0ef-f2081cc85fef" :answer-field/key "$A$ is **not** invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "873e0c05-9845-5591-87a1-097a96eb6fbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451757} {:answer/id #uuid "5eba92ea-50a0-54c0-aba7-d88034bc70b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "873e0c05-9845-5591-87a1-097a96eb6fbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451757} :answer-field/id #uuid "c26a036b-3629-5b64-969c-37e14040c238" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452726}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "92ccb45d-8792-5a6a-9a10-b7498ac220cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-79423" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\right\\}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=4=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\right\\}=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=4,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is **not** invertible” is true. Indeed, since $\\text{rank}(A)=1\\ne 4,$ it follows, by the invertible matrix theorem, that the matrix $A$ is *not* invertible.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{4}$” is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=1$ then $\\text{Col}(A)$ is, in fact,  a $1$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is **not** invertible” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce3c5f0-7529-5c2c-9564-44c889eb86c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453386} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0a7954-cd05-51a7-90b9-b780bf965f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ce3c5f0-7529-5c2c-9564-44c889eb86c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453386} :answer-field/id #uuid "bca78a15-c48c-5741-abab-0bf7b97a57a4" :answer-field/key "The number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454443} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcec78e2-d6bb-56c4-ad75-975ad764b8c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453388} {:answer/id #uuid "292a5262-ac7c-5df9-a70a-6d1d92a3b30d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcec78e2-d6bb-56c4-ad75-975ad764b8c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453388} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd94f480-acd9-57b8-a0ef-b55824c69c2f" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454444} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dd8e82d-abc1-543c-9e38-eb7d06e6eeb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453390} {:answer/id #uuid "399ad536-9e21-50bb-b29b-6a5685869bad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "399ad536-9e21-50bb-b29b-6a5685869bad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453391} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcdeb836-29c1-560f-b756-552781011c7f" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454445}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8048be79-9af8-51c0-a0c1-5b68f549139c" :question/math-academy-id "q-139986" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=4=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $3$” is false. Since the generating vectors in \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}\n$$\n\nare linearly independent, we conclude that the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $1.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$ is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=1\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=4.$ Now, according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9290da55-a6a3-5bb8-a9b8-2039b243ee6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453404} {:answer/id #uuid "adeaa133-0730-51b1-8b37-ab1eabd66c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adeaa133-0730-51b1-8b37-ab1eabd66c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453405} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f82a48-c4e0-5658-a295-60736c7e5166" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454452} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88d7d24f-3606-50eb-9098-a34319240958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453406} {:answer/id #uuid "535a174d-2f6e-5ab0-99bb-3ccad768cc35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88d7d24f-3606-50eb-9098-a34319240958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453406} :answer-field/id #uuid "59aa5f02-f270-5643-aeca-3ee7824a7629" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454453} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99558d31-6961-52e7-b662-299510c283b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453408} {:answer/id #uuid "688a37cc-bcaf-529c-a80d-90d43dc9aa3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99558d31-6961-52e7-b662-299510c283b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453408} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f387ba8-880e-5912-8b03-6a51150d10c2" :answer-field/key "$A$ is  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454454}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "017db163-2592-561e-a975-d762dc265a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-142542" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is true. Indeed, since\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=5,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =5 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}$ is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=2\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is  invertible” is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=3\\ne 5$, according to the  invertible matrix theorem $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee3ba979-73eb-55d9-98be-53eb63f15310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454018} {:answer/id #uuid "42f7e70e-a33c-5389-83b8-4b66c4b40413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42f7e70e-a33c-5389-83b8-4b66c4b40413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454019} :answer-field/id #uuid "51beb1c0-c434-5ffe-be4f-d1af3a966f94" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b27c5d69-4610-55e4-befd-bab1f9f21b77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454020} {:answer/id #uuid "7f38039b-9493-5449-afe0-51512728ff71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f38039b-9493-5449-afe0-51512728ff71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454021} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd2f4dc-0220-560a-b969-e0fb63f01a28" :answer-field/key "$A$ is not  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22168706-fdd0-5ec9-8357-a478a254b0de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454022} {:answer/id #uuid "b3eaef39-5ed2-5d0e-8448-e5d92a445686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22168706-fdd0-5ec9-8357-a478a254b0de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454022} :answer-field/id #uuid "447c453c-9c02-53db-ad8b-23d0593303f4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454761}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c7ff497-8845-5d34-a5a1-e0b10d7a1e25" :question/math-academy-id "q-79367" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix with $3$ pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is true. Indeed, since $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is not  invertible” is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=5.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$ is false. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)=3$; “$A$ is not  invertible” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491ec8ca-40f3-5454-809e-b6b418901802" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489686} {:answer/id #uuid "4bad21d3-8ccb-5f2e-b04d-bc4550a71c3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489691} {:answer/id #uuid "83029887-1c17-5621-b865-840b4e1ed3fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489813} {:answer/id #uuid "8884a0e0-0a83-5ace-92f9-fb64604eefa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489827} {:answer/id #uuid "916469af-a06a-5bf7-a441-a7fdd789fe00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8884a0e0-0a83-5ace-92f9-fb64604eefa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489827} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6251f1-889c-581d-b906-e6b75fa33975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490134}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "128f0273-6319-516f-a4e8-3d58e084f0a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-142538" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix with $2$ pivot columns?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{5} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false.  Since $A$ has $2$ pivot columns, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=5.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have that $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 2+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490316 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "298c6536-dd07-5d51-8c18-8ca670439c0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489607} {:answer/id #uuid "37b42792-707d-5224-838b-cff46365c833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489639} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec0644e-4274-5048-9b84-1b7e49ed7bcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489741} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a192c7-d581-5aec-87a2-1e74c429a5b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489985} {:answer/id #uuid "df796ca4-fa04-56be-ad9e-bc125d4ef4a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37b42792-707d-5224-838b-cff46365c833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489639} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ea1ac60-40da-5758-9bc0-142c36f8f6ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490155}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e3a4804f-9ed9-56b0-80c9-162f94bd57af" :question/math-academy-id "q-79411" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix which has exactly $2$ non-pivot columns?\n\nI. $A$ is  invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{6} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $A$ has $n=6$ columns and $2$ of them are non-pivot ones, it follows that    \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6-2=4\\ne 6.\n$$\n\n Thus, according to the invertible matrix theorem $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=4$,  then $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $n=6$, according to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =6 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f279b3-ea5e-5d31-9dcd-0a3e8e1b3a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522038} {:answer/id #uuid "2c39de95-065d-5909-a31e-8aec18fcaa30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522120} {:answer/id #uuid "5c15ec5b-b014-5f4f-aedd-7a3ee80c6e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522210} {:answer/id #uuid "c65ee4e2-e412-5286-95cc-2961eb9dd28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522434} {:answer/id #uuid "daf23a31-b6e9-551f-8960-6733a9da0c3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09f279b3-ea5e-5d31-9dcd-0a3e8e1b3a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522038} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf7368f2-5a45-59f1-9769-661d58ae07d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522656}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c579df31-38e7-5faa-a719-e9a3badf209e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35435" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ -4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?$ \n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$\n\nIII. $A$ is not invertible" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ -4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}=\\text{Span}\\{\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=1.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=4,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=3\\ne 4,$ then, by the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $\\text{rank}(A)=3\\ne 4$, according to the  invertible matrix theorem $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f1b4ae3-0a40-5756-bb35-332f91366150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545226} {:answer/id #uuid "341ea572-fea0-5ab5-8e97-94b9de3afc39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545303} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc8c0b7-7f8f-5ba1-a69b-9e3d9da97a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545318} {:answer/id #uuid "73232096-0842-59cd-811b-a3783597953d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545416} {:answer/id #uuid "855804bf-27d3-5391-ba94-a4c1ff073b30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f1b4ae3-0a40-5756-bb35-332f91366150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545226} :answer-field/id #uuid "c143e0e6-92b8-5ab3-a31a-0f6f3f8892c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545765}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c10d4c77-93c5-52a9-900d-275fa9299d3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-79410" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{4}$\n\nIII. $A$ has $2$ pivot colums" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since the non-zero vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nspans $\\text{Null}(A),$ we conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=1.$ So, by the rank-nullity theorem, with $n=4$,  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=\\text{rank}(A)=3,$ we must have  that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The fact that $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=3$ implies that the number of pivot columns in $A$ is also equal to $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186601938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f5fb18-cd10-50a1-804b-52cc7bd09f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601603} {:answer/id #uuid "34213afb-951e-586a-910f-32f76d572451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601633} {:answer/id #uuid "4b033259-ad61-5852-b7ae-4c69d95eadda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601649} {:answer/id #uuid "be45a3e2-f6af-5a5c-8b30-6476c2da97d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601756} {:answer/id #uuid "f135b625-3a56-594d-83f9-4191b8a5a9e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f135b625-3a56-594d-83f9-4191b8a5a9e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601795} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c2ff09e-a029-5cda-a90b-ac45f62f8970" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186601827}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c935622f-4794-551b-bc04-e73546072768" :question/math-academy-id "q-35424" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?$ \n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$  \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}=\\text{Span}\\{\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=1.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=3,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =3 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =3-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=1\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible we must have   $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d4fbbca-395d-5779-ad55-5f2dfe894b9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673419} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e4d0f2-e20d-593d-8147-2516d450feb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d4fbbca-395d-5779-ad55-5f2dfe894b9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673419} :answer-field/id #uuid "659ec4e5-fea1-5cd9-a3bc-edb596a4a35d" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08e87190-2841-5611-9c70-dc6033a40400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673408} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b668ec-e524-508e-93cd-8eb84b3df602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08e87190-2841-5611-9c70-dc6033a40400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673408} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1c24042-b870-5f0a-80ac-f4818e90caf5" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $5$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673435} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2390ff3f-82fc-54bf-9b85-5082cf00aedd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673414} {:answer/id #uuid "2b01ce81-b96e-5329-acb7-60b29187eee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2390ff3f-82fc-54bf-9b85-5082cf00aedd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673414} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba2b51a4-1c12-534c-8dce-a26aa8889459" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673442}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01c27acc-5739-59f4-8fe9-e2185b961d5f" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix which has only $5$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 5 non-pivot columns give $\\text{nullity}(A)=5.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+5=5,\\qquad \\text{rank}(A)=5-5=0.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=0$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 0. The number of pivot columns is 0, and the number of non-pivot columns is 5.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $5$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{5}.$” is false. $\\dim(\\text{Col}(A))=0$.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(A)=5$” is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "366e42cb-2574-576c-ae6c-5df19e16a5c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673418} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b4a4ea-a7da-5796-ba31-4f54586baecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1b4a4ea-a7da-5796-ba31-4f54586baecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673439} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aff7ca8-ae95-5320-870a-283e02efa317" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673412} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b9502c-410e-52f5-b026-c2f9b31705b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673417} {:answer/id #uuid "a1dc0d68-471b-5062-b20b-5752e4b0dd3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1dc0d68-471b-5062-b20b-5752e4b0dd3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673436} :answer-field/id #uuid "49d0098d-44ad-5e1e-85dd-1dbbc7334091" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=8$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673421} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9efa1286-95cb-5e3d-9779-3876fa3adc06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673434} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a03354-d256-5b30-83a7-5851e5a7b6ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9efa1286-95cb-5e3d-9779-3876fa3adc06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673434} :answer-field/id #uuid "68418815-8305-5b5e-9da2-656a31ba6134" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673429}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a6f89b5-17bd-5c0c-b910-92e1887d4880" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix with $2$ pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $10\\times 10$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{10} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=10=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 2 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n2+\\text{nullity}(A)=10,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=10-2=8.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 2. The number of pivot columns is 2, and the number of non-pivot columns is 8.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(A)=8$” is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{rank}(A)=2$” is true. $\\text{rank}(A)=2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{nullity}(A)=8$; $\\text{rank}(A)=2$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673413 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12f8229f-ef39-5cfa-a4bd-a0f2f936e940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673410} {:answer/id #uuid "47514b44-7fec-5627-8a5b-bcce4012cc85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673420} {:answer/id #uuid "a327f0df-7451-5065-ba8a-d07d7567aa5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673437} {:answer/id #uuid "d8369a5b-132b-5815-ac55-3ca829df5152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673449} {:answer/id #uuid "de9acc3e-1ada-5d6a-9abe-29947f31aa9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47514b44-7fec-5627-8a5b-bcce4012cc85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673420} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b95a80-6d17-56c6-be43-c7d7451f84eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673407}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c93f8c9-c546-50e4-a1df-c54e8f82f0eb" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix with $3$ pivot columns?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=5$\n\nII. $A$ is not invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=1$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$\\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{8} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 3 pivot columns give $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n3+\\text{nullity}(A)=8,\\qquad \\text{nullity}(A)=8-3=5.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 3. The number of pivot columns is 3, and the number of non-pivot columns is 5.\n\n- Statement I is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement III is false. $\\text{nullity}(A)=5$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is II only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd61621-e086-56a9-ae64-6d28ed6d1944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673427} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad663d6-03d5-593b-8d23-be79be698d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ad663d6-03d5-593b-8d23-be79be698d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673432} :answer-field/id #uuid "54107d25-70b8-589c-83d0-fde2f4e5a0fb" :answer-field/key "$A$ is not invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673424} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12d11e7b-2e35-5882-ae11-4fee9d03b2dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673409} {:answer/id #uuid "f27e0ecc-9ad0-52b4-9fc9-97c1ee550c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f27e0ecc-9ad0-52b4-9fc9-97c1ee550c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673451} :answer-field/id #uuid "a989528a-e5a8-5859-bd54-1f3759ea645b" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673438} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c3b4623-c248-5a02-b8ee-7ba16209f579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673416} {:answer/id #uuid "bd48ae13-0ac2-55cd-85b8-8715b9df1712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c3b4623-c248-5a02-b8ee-7ba16209f579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673416} :answer-field/id #uuid "b207d561-698d-59e0-a012-bb9ff356ca43" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673440}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b807f80-d3e7-5284-9d78-b367cb5db361" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $\\text{Null}(A)=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2a \\\\ 3a \\\\ 3b\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,a,b\\in R\\right\\}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{3} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=3=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$  \n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe supplied null space has the independent spanning vectors\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\;\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThus $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+2=3,\\qquad \\text{rank}(A)=3-2=1.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=1$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 1. The number of pivot columns is 1, and the number of non-pivot columns is 2.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is not invertible” is true. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{rank}(A)=0$” is false. $\\text{rank}(A)=1$.\n\n- Statement “$det(A)=0$” is true. $A$ is not invertible, so $\\det(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A$ is not invertible; $det(A)=0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bf661d7-522d-523e-924c-cf70e56ef4c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673422} {:answer/id #uuid "50595a0f-e68c-5eb9-8d4e-509557233567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bf661d7-522d-523e-924c-cf70e56ef4c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673422} :answer-field/id #uuid "56e65182-7ecd-5970-9716-4a82b7f451d7" :answer-field/key "$A$ is not invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673425} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cdb4946-a773-51de-8878-8b57d29bd2a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673430} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4ad4a5-953b-533a-8148-f2399789ddb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cdb4946-a773-51de-8878-8b57d29bd2a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673430} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e9d96e5-a8d2-524c-9ca1-ee4d9e72432e" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673431} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb6ddb6a-a2fb-5bdc-afea-25f9024d2e18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673443} {:answer/id #uuid "cba8c704-e212-5518-be74-5971633bb01d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb6ddb6a-a2fb-5bdc-afea-25f9024d2e18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673443} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ec3bf1-9be3-5daa-bfbb-855721c618f1" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673441}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7fdbf75-0d39-5481-92c5-3bb3459c2aeb" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix which has only $2$ non-pivot column?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible\n\n$$\n\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{7} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=7=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nThe 2 non-pivot columns give $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nBy the rank-nullity theorem,\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+2=7,\\qquad \\text{rank}(A)=7-2=5.\n$$\n\nHence $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ and $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$. Since rank is less than the number of columns, $A$ is not invertible and $\\det(A)=0$. Also, $\\text{Col}(A)$ has dimension 5. The number of pivot columns is 5, and the number of non-pivot columns is 2.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is not invertible” is true. The rank is less than the number of columns.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is a $3$-dimensional subspace of ${R}^{7}.$” is false. $\\dim(\\text{Col}(A))=5$.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{nullity}(A)=2$” is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A$ is not invertible; $\\text{nullity}(A)=2$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem and the Rank-Nullity Theorem"}]}
